%% EMBRACE research-inspired defensive trust-boundary model, 2026-10-29
%% Conceptual architecture; NOT an OpenAI/VS Code implementation diagram.
flowchart LR
    U["Developer"] --> REPO["Untrusted repository / downloaded HTML"]
    REPO --> GATE{"Preview policy gate"}
    GATE -->|"Untrusted or unknown"| ISO["Disposable VM / isolated standard browser"]
    GATE -->|"Approved project only"| AGENT["AI coding agent"]
    AGENT --> PREVIEW["Embedded preview / browser"]
    PREVIEW -->|"Potential boundary: local file reads"| FS["Developer workstation filesystem"]
    FS --> SEC["Secrets: SSH keys / tokens / .env"]
    PREVIEW -->|"Potential boundary: network egress"| NET["External network"]
    ISO --> MON["Telemetry and policy logs"]
    AGENT --> MON
    PREVIEW --> MON
    FS --> MON
    MON --> SOC["Security monitoring / incident response"]
    VAULT["Scoped short-lived credentials / secret manager"] -.-> AGENT
    POLICY["Endpoint inventory + least-privilege policy"] -.-> GATE
    POLICY -.-> AGENT
    POLICY -.-> PREVIEW

    subgraph DEVICE["Developer endpoint — privileged trust zone"]
        AGENT
        PREVIEW
        FS
        SEC
        MON
    end
    subgraph OUTSIDE["Lower-trust content and external destinations"]
        REPO
        ISO
        NET
    end

    classDef danger fill:#fee2e2,stroke:#b91c1c,color:#7f1d1d
    classDef control fill:#dcfce7,stroke:#166534,color:#14532d
    class PREVIEW,FS,SEC,NET danger
    class GATE,ISO,VAULT,POLICY,MON,SOC control
